marie_cs: FYI onboarding account 'aurora' reporting bursty 429s + occasional 401s when users background/foreground the mobile app. Started after they upgraded to our mobile SDK.

devon_eng: Which mobile SDK and what auth flow are they using? 401s + 429s suggests token churn + parallel preflight/refresh.

marie_cs: They use our iOS SDK v0.9.8 and issue ephemeral tokens from their backend (ttl=20s). App does a token refresh on resume and also starts a preflight when the SDK inits.

riley_oncall: That TTL is tiny for mobile. If many users background+resume around same time (push wakeups, OS scheduling), you'll get token refresh storms. Any service-worker-like background syncs?

marie_cs: Not SW but background fetch on iOS and some in-app cron that wakes every minute. Logs: `HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests - {"error":"rate_limit_exceeded","scope":"preflight","retry_after":3}` and intermittent `401 {"error":"invalid_token"}`.

devon_eng: v0.9.8 had a known double-init on app resume where SDK init + manual refresh triggered preflight twice. We patched that in 0.10.4. Immediate mitigations: increase token TTL to >=60s, centralize refresh to a single background task, and add exponential jitter on refresh. Also set PREFLIGHT_DEDUP_WINDOW_MS=500 to coalesce near-simultaneous preflights.

marie_cs: Customer asked for repro steps so they can test. I spun a k6 script that simulates RNG wakeups across 500 clients and saw the same 429 spike. Repro snippet:```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export default function() {
  // simulate random wakeups and refresh storms
  if (Math.random() < 0.05) {
    http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/token/refresh', JSON.stringify({uid: Math.floor(Math.random()*10000)}), { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }});
  }
  http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/preflight', JSON.stringify({model: 'gpt-x'}), { headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer <ephemeral>' }});
  sleep(Math.random()*2);
}
```

riley_oncall: Ops note: also check their CDN/edge config. We once saw a CloudFront cache TTL misconfig that made many clients bypass edge caching and hit origin concurrently. That amplifies the load. Look for identical User-Agent bursts in gateway logs.

devon_eng: Short-term patches to push to customer: 1) set token TTL >= 60s 2) bump SDK to 0.10.4 (contains resume/dedup fixes) 3) enable PREFLIGHT_DEDUP_WINDOW_MS=500 and PREFLIGHT_BACKOFF_BASE_MS=200 4) centralize token refresh on a single background queue and add randomness.

marie_cs: Sent the checklist to the customer and asked for a test window. They applied TTL=90s + PREFLIGHT_DEDUP_WINDOW_MS=500 and ran the k6 repro for 30 minutes; they reported 0 429s. Monitoring for 2 hours. :white_check_mark:

release-bot: release: sdk@0.10.4 deployed to canary (job 4387) - includes preflight dedup and resume-fix.

riley_oncall: Please add a short KB: "Mobile SDK: avoid short ephemeral TTLs; centralize refresh; enable preflight dedup" and a note to default PREFLIGHT_DEDUP_WINDOW_MS to 500 in next SDK minor. +1 from infra. :thumbsup:

devon_eng: I'll follow up and draft the KB. Also flag to Product: consider telemetry that surfaces client-side refresh storms in Console (token-refresh rate by app version).

marie_cs: Thanks all. I'll update the account health board and mark "at risk" -> "stabilizing" once the 2h window is clean.
